commit d76742b135169b7ba9653a94cd345d34aae2da49
Author: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>
Date:   Wed Jun 10 06:11:47 2026 +1000

    Use importlib.metadata to read openstacksdk version.

    openstacksdk has dropped its internal import of the deprecated
    openstack.version submodule (commit 3ae89d61 "drop deprecated
    openstack.version", 2026-06-02). That import was the side effect
    that made openstack.version reachable as an attribute on the
    openstack package; with it gone, any consumer that reads
    openstack.version.__version__ now fails with:

        AttributeError: module 'openstack' has no attribute 'version'

    This collection hit that failure in three places:

    * plugins/module_utils/openstack.py (legacy
        openstack_cloud_from_module function)
    * plugins/module_utils/openstack.py (OpenStackModule class)
    * plugins/inventory/openstack.py

    Switch all three call sites to importlib.metadata.version and
    packaging call to get base_version, which is the canonical Python
    way of reading an installed distribution's version and will omit
    pbr generated versioning like "1.1.1.dev11"

    Change-Id: I8b6a1c5d5f4d6111e3f83e6a668a812d6fd2449b
    Signed-off-by: Michael Still <mikal@stillhq.com>

diff --git a/changelogs/fragments/use_importlib_metadata_for_sdk_version.yaml b/changelogs/fragments/use_importlib_metadata_for_sdk_version.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..fa7abfb3bb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelogs/fragments/use_importlib_metadata_for_sdk_version.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+---
+bugfixes:
+  - Replace use of the deprecated ``openstack.version`` submodule with
+    ``importlib.metadata.version('openstacksdk')`` when looking up the
+    installed openstacksdk version. The previous code relied on
+    openstacksdk's internal import of its own ``version`` submodule as a
+    side effect to expose ``openstack.version`` as a package attribute.
+    openstacksdk has now dropped that internal usage, causing
+    ``AttributeError: module 'openstack' has no attribute 'version'`` in
+    any module or in the inventory plugin that talks to a cloud.
diff --git a/ci/run-ansible-tests-collection.sh b/ci/run-ansible-tests-collection.sh
index cd31cf13c2..ffee97eddd 100755
--- a/ci/run-ansible-tests-collection.sh
+++ b/ci/run-ansible-tests-collection.sh
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@ for var in $(env | grep -e '^ANSIBLE_VAR_'); do
 done
 
 # Discover openstacksdk version
-SDK_VER=$(python -c "import openstack; print(openstack.version.__version__)")
+SDK_VER=$(python -c "import importlib.metadata; print(importlib.metadata.version('openstacksdk'))")
 
 # Choose integration tests
 tag_opt=""
